 "equipment_type": "Evaporative condenser controller",
 "applies_to": "Johnson Controls / Frick XLP3b evaporative condensers for industrial refrigeration with the factory PLC control panel (up to eight fans and a pump).",
 "summary": "The XLP3b control panel exposes a small BACnet IP object set for the BMS: unit status and alarm, a BMS enable, fan and pump run commands, a fan speed setpoint, fan and pump run status, the speed sent to the fans, and for each of up to eight fans its run status, speed feedback, alarm and an override. The same points are also available over Modbus TCP.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Access is from the R/W column. The IOM says only IP based protocols are supported.",
  "Fan objects follow a per-fan pattern: fan n uses BV n0 (run status), AV n0 (speed), BV n1 (alarm) and BV n2 (override), for n = 1 to 8.",
  "Fan speed feedback is in rpm per the Modbus table; the BMS fan speed command is a percent.",
  "Defaults: BMS Enable, fan and pump commands and the fan speed command are 0; the fan overrides default to 1 (normal).",
  "An evaporative condenser condenses refrigerant from an industrial refrigeration system; it is not a cooling tower or fluid cooler."
 ],
